{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 130,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Flying in a 747 from one side of the earth\nto the exact opposite side would take about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4580,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "22 hours…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5580,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and while I know there's a bit of rock in\nthe way, that's really going the long way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8630,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "round."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9780,
    "dDurationMs": 4319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what if we did dig a hole all the way through\nthe earth, through the center, and jumped"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14099,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15099,
    "dDurationMs": 3821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, Michael, you probably would't make it\nvery far - that's because of the Coriolis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18920,
    "dDurationMs": 3769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "effect (which is why a ball curves weirdly\nwhen you toss it while riding a merry go round"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22689,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and why hurricanes always spin counterclockwise\nin the northern hemisphere)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25919,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the equator, the earth (and you on it)\nis rotating eastwards at 1670 km/hr."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30179,
    "dDurationMs": 4791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you go deeper, the bits of earth around\nyou are still spinning around once per day,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34970,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they don't have as far to travel so they're\ngoing at slower and slower speeds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38070,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you jumped into a vertical shaft, you'd\nsoon be traveling east faster than the rock"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42170,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around you so that after falling only a few\nkilometers, you'd crash into the eastern wall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46090,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It might not be a disaster, but some miners\nnear Lake Superior tried to test this by dropping"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50250,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cannon balls down a mile-long shaft - and\nthe balls never reached the bottom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54040,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OK, so what if the tunnel went from pole to\npole, so the Coriolis effect didn't apply,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59860,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and let's also assume that there's no air\nresistance, or friction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64260,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65260,
    "dDurationMs": 3399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since the earth's mass is more concentrated\nclose to the middle, gravity would pull you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68659,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down with roughly the same amount of force\nfor the first 3000 km, or halfway to the center"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71509,
    "dDurationMs": 3411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the earth - this familiar, constant force\nwould accelerate you until you were falling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74920,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "8km every second, and the trip halfway to\nthe middle of the earth would only take 13"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79479,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "minutes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80479,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Soon after, you'd reach the earth's outer\ncore, and this is the point in your journey"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83539,
    "dDurationMs": 3731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the pull of gravity would be strongest\n- but only slightly stronger than the force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87270,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're used to on the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89000,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you continued to fall closer to the center,\nso much of the earth's mass would now be above"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92709,
    "dDurationMs": 3351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you that it would begin to seriously cancel\nout the attraction of the mass below, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96060,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the pull would weaken until you reached the\ncenter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98700,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, you'd experience no gravitational pull\nat all - or rather, the earth would be pulling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102950,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on you the same amount in all directions,\nso you could float freely around with no sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106899,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of \"up\" or \"down\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108869,
    "dDurationMs": 4221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except, remember, that you'd be speeding past\nat 22,000 miles per hour, or 6 miles a second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113090,
    "dDurationMs": 3659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once you passed the center, the whole process\nwould reverse and you'd gradually slow, pulled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116749,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down (or is it up?) weakly at first and then\nmore strongly, until when you got to the other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121179,
    "dDurationMs": 4141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "side, you'd stop moving and could step out\non the surface, a mere 37 minutes, or one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125320,
    "dDurationMs": 2339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dryer cycle, later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127659,
    "dDurationMs": 5251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, the deepest we've ever been able\nto dig is the Kola Superdeep borehole in Russia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132910,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it only went down 12km, which is only\ntwo thirds the length of Manhattan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139270,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had to stop because it got too hot: 180°C.\nAnd this is sort of the problem with digging"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144810,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a hole through earth - earth is hot, and molten\nin the middle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148880,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't just dig a hole through it with\nshovels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150740,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here's a question: wasn't the middle of\nearth wasn't all \"liquidy\", what if earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156240,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was hollow, but weighed the same?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159690,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, with its entire mass concentrated in\na thin shell right under our feet, the earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164000,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wouldn't have a magnetic field any more, because\nthat comes from the molten iron core."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167780,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we'd be totally vulnerable to radiation\nfrom the solar wind and storms, and this means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171880,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'd see the aurora EVERYWHERE."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173460,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Look!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174460,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The NorthernSouthernEastern lights!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176120,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you jumped inside the hollow earth\nto escape the solar storm?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179310,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, gravity from the different parts of\nthe spherical earth-shell would perfectly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182690,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cancel out and you'd float freely about inside\nas if the earth weren't there at all!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186610,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, you'd better bring a space suit,\nbecause there's not nearly enough air ON earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190300,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fill up the entire INSIDE of earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192630,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what if the entire inside of the hollow\nearth were covered with mirrors?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195990,
    "dDurationMs": 3490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry, that's ridiculous… for now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199480,
    "dDurationMs": 6340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so back outside of the earth, we wouldn't\nreally notice much difference from a gravitational"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205820,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perspective - falling things would still accelerate\nat 9.8 m/s^2, a baseball would follow the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210620,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same trajectory, and the moon would follow\nthe same orbit around the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215060,
    "dDurationMs": 3290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey Henry, let's go to outer space, right\nnow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218350,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bring your gun - this'll all make sense later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221590,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "C'mon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222740,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, and you're coming too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224970,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Click this annotation to head over to my channel,\nVsauce, to see the rest of our adventures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228470,
    "dDurationMs": 3019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'll see you over there."
    } ]
  } ]
}
